  "aciklama": "USS Thresher was lost during a deep-diving test. The cause: probable flooding from a piping joint, reactor shutdown, and ice blocking the emergency ballast blow.\n\nFailure chain: Likely pipe joint leak → Reactor shuts down → Emergency blow attempted → Ice blocks air strainers → Sub sinks past crush depth\n\nRelated episode: General Slocum: The Inspection That Killed — https://youtu.be/NnGoWJOdaW0\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Ships searching for USS Thresher (SSN-593), 15 April 1963 (NH 97555).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ships_searching_for_USS_Thresher_(SSN-593)%2C_15_April_1963_(NH_97555).jpg\n• Archival film: \"USS Thresher (SSN-593) debris.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USS_Thresher_(SSN-593)_debris.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Amerikaanse atoomduikboot Thesher met 129 man vermist, Bestanddeelnr 915-0380.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amerikaanse_atoomduikboot_Thesher_met_129_man_vermist%2C_Bestanddeelnr_915-0380.jpg\n• Archival film: \"USS Thresher (SSN-593) sonar dome.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USS_Thresher_(SSN-593)_sonar_dome.jpg\n• Archival film: \"USS Thresher memorial dedication at Arlington.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USS_Thresher_memorial_dedication_at_Arlington.jpg\n• Archival film: \"330-PSA-110-63 (USN 711302) (22171571340).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:330-PSA-110-63_(USN_711302)_(22171571340).jpg\n• Archival film: \"330-PSA-110-63 (USN 711303) (22172737989).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:330-PSA-110-63_(USN_711303)_(22172737989).jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — USS Thresher (SSN-593) — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USS_Thresher_(SSN-593)\n• Government source — THRESHER pg 1 300 (cited by Wikipedia) — https://www.secnav.navy.mil/foia/readingroom/HotTopics/THRESHER%20RELEASE/THRESHER%20pg%201-300.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\nFailure File · Episode 17 · A new engineering failure, reconstructed every day.\n\n#shorts #engineering #USSThresher #maritime #history",
